  "title": "Using ICE Charts: Part II",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "ICE charts allow you to make inferences about equilibrium concentrations which can be used to solve for unknowns. However, ICE charts do not always result in being able to determine a specific value for equilibrium concentrations as we saw in the previous examples. Let's take a look at some examples."
              }
            ],
            "id": "lxb5gqevr8x2158",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3635778274",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Hydrogen gas and Iodine gas react to form Hydrogen iodide gas according to the equation below:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ljjrrfs2m5n3vin",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "hitv3ap782jhwno",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wa0l2dc4n88fpfd",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm I}_2(g)\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{HI}(g)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "1.50 mol of H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(g) and 1.00 mol I"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(g) are mixed in a 1.00 L container at a certain temperature. At this temperature the equilibrium constant is 1.00 x 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Calculate the concentrations of each species once the system reaches equilibrium."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "953ye0jzymfqbt0",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Write the equilibrium expression, including the given value for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "c"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "x0mh4k3edh45y9f",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ythizvyo9kanjuo",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2itldepbme5m87y",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "K_c\\;=\\;\\frac{\\lbrack\\mathrm{HI}\\rbrack^2}{\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_2\\rbrack\\lbrack{\\mathrm I}_2\\rbrack}\\;=\\;1.00\\times10^2",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Here we are given a value for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "c"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", but no equilibrium concentrations. We will need to use an ICE chart. Enter the initial concentrations given in the problem."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "bkjn20e8lfbv8al",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
