                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", we can plug the equilibrium concentrations from the ICE table into the equilibrium expression to determine the value of x."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "tzx020kx4x12gj8",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "tawg8vdbtrw7a4o",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3ph3utriy3zcisq",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "K_c\\;=\\;\\frac{\\lbrack\\mathrm{HI}\\rbrack^2}{\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_2\\rbrack\\lbrack{\\mathrm I}_2\\rbrack}\\;=\\;1.00\\times10^2",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "osbdgu68hpc095a",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "8pfqbks5rnp4v4c",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "1.00\\times10^2\\;=\\;\\frac{(2\\mathrm x)^2}{(1.5\\;-\\;\\mathrm x)(1.0\\;-\\;\\mathrm x)}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "This equation contains only one variable, "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "x"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", the change in concentration. We can write the equation as a quadratic equation and solve for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "x"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " using the quadratic formula."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "nqq98a5gdbgx7yb",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "yhdkqyhn396q74n",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "isbkxui4wg68oyh",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}100\\;=\\;\\frac{(2x)^2}{(1.5\\;-\\;x)(1.0\\;-\\;x)}\\\\100(x^2\\;-\\;2.5\\;x\\;+\\;1.5)\\;=\\;4x^2\\\\100x^2\\;-\\;250\\;x\\;+\\;150\\;=\\;4x^2\\\\96x^2\\;-\\;250\\;x\\;+\\;150\\;=\\;0\\;\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The quadratic equation can be used to solve for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "x"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xmxrky3bf1fstw7",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "0t3k2dj4h9v4tuv",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "mdfd8v3hartpm1v",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "x\\;=\\;\\frac{-b\\;\\pm\\;\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "In this case, a = 96, b = -250, and c = 150. Substituting the appropriate values for a, b, and c yields:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "r7982qfm88gsqnn",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ejkimub3gm37fz1",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xt9fmlwgcg4vjld",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}x\\;=\\;\\frac{250\\;\\pm\\;\\sqrt{(-250)^2\\;-\\;4(96)(150)}}{2\\;\\cdot\\;96}\\\\\\\\x\\;=\\;\\frac{250\\;\\pm\\;\\sqrt{4900}}{192}\\\\\\\\x\\;=\\;0.9375\\\\or\\;\\\\x\\;=\\;1.667\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Quadratic equations often have two different solutions, one that is physically possible and one that is physically impossible (an extraneous root). In this case, the second solution (1.667) is physically impossible because this would give an equilibrium concentration for [I"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] of 1.0 - 1.667 = -0.667. Since concentrations cannot be negative values, we know this is the extraneous root."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "sb1k6ibtyp226yg",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Given the x = 0.9375, we can use the value to calculate equilibrium concentrations."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2igj0tzpztraiz5",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "wst3mmdg8jsis6z",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "heubbmsjgdolduj",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_2\\rbrack\\;=\\;1.50\\;-\\;0.9375\\;=\\;0.562\\;\\mathrm M\\\\\\\\\\lbrack{\\mathrm I}_2\\rbrack\\;=\\;1.00\\;-\\;0.9375\\;=\\;0.0625\\;\\mathrm M\\\\\\\\\\lbrack\\mathrm{HI}\\rbrack\\;=\\;2\\;(0.9375)\\;=\\;1.88\\;\\mathrm M\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              }
            ],
            "id": "692877782",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  1,
                  0
                ]
              }
            },
            "type": "content"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3012780750",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "example",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "a4tjkd4qyrnng3v",
                "text": "Interactive Example: Equilibrium Concentrations"
              }
            ],
            "id": "t8g3p23zz3f7xkw",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "What are the concentrations of all species after a mixture that contains [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "O] = 1.00 M and [Cl"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "O] = 0.500 M comes to equilibrium?"
              }
            ],
            "id": "58038m2atjvdjyt",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "bpm6498mmlx6oi2",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "je6hjb9rxz97kak",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm{Cl}}_2\\mathrm O(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{HOCl}(g)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K_c=0.900",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "615nup25l4k9rni",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "height": "470",
            "id": "7xhsi36fdcz1oib",
            "src": "https://h5p.org/h5p/embed/200013",
            "type": "iframe",
            "width": "800"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3034989193",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
