            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Carbon monoxide (CO) and chlorine gas (Cl"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") are used to prepare phosgene (COCl"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "). A chemical used in the manufacture of plastics. "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "n2a2la4ig5qd7pi",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "h9b2yf0yxjg5q83",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "slsxytgt1nx0klx",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{CO}(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm{Cl}}_2(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm{COCl}}_2(g)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K_c\\;=\\;1230",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "0.380 M CO is mixed with 0.393 M Cl"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in an evacuated container. What are the equilibrium concentrations of each species?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "dzugl7lyiof9213",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
